DATASETS (coding-agent final messages)
--------------------------------------
moth's "agent companion" training used real final messages from public coding-agent traces: the last message
an agent wrote to its user at the end of a run.

Changes made: each message was cleaned before use. Markdown was stripped (code blocks replaced by "[code]",
inline code, tables, headings, emphasis and links removed), whitespace was collapsed, and long messages were
truncated to their first 110 and last 45 words. The cleaned messages were used as prompts: the teacher model
wrote moth's reactions to them, and those chats became training data. The raw messages are not part of the
model.

Exception: code/data/eval_agent_msgs.json redistributes 40 messages unmodified, each with its source dataset
and row index (30 from lambda/hermes-agent-reasoning-traces, 7 from nvidia/Nemotron-SWE-v1, 3 from
nebius/SWE-rebench-openhands-trajectories). The evaluation scripts use them as test prompts.

