ARTWORK (desktop pet, Petdex sprite sheet, chat page icon)
---------------------------------------------------------
The moth that the desktop pet (code/moth/pet.py) shows, the sprite sheet that `python -m moth.pet
--export-petdex` writes, and the chat page's header icon and favicon (code/moth/static/index.html) all use the
art below. It is not covered by this repository's Apache-2.0 license. The original SVG and a full credit list are
in code/moth/assets/ (CREDITS.md).

202206 Silkmoth adult female icon, by DataBase Center for Life Science (DBCLS), doi:10.7875/togopic.2022.231
  Source:  https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:202206_Silkmoth_adult_female_icon.svg
  License: CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
  Changes: the pet renders the SVG and cuts it along the body into two wings and the body (a clip polygon that
           follows the body's outline). Its wing-flap, resting and dozing frames squash the wings toward the body
           and turn them a few degrees. The frames are scaled and leaned toward the flight direction, and the
           Petdex export packs them into the Petdex 8x9 grid. The page inlines the SVG with rounded coordinates
           and fill attributes in place of classes, clips it into the same three parts so CSS can flap the wings,
           and uses a 64x64 PNG rendering as its favicon. Nothing was drawn new. The original SVG is included
           unmodified (code/moth/assets/silkmoth_adult_female_icon.svg).


